    <text>
        <front>
            <div type="summary">
                <p>
                    <persName key="MAPP0057">B. A. Strange</persName> wrote to <persName key="MAPP0058">Monica Stirling</persName> about an issue 
                    regarding the royalties involving the book <title level="m">La Mort de la Phalene</title>.
                </p>
            </div>
        </front>
        <body>
            <div type="letter">
                <opener>
                    <dateline>
                        <date when="1976-04-21">
                            21st April 1976
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                    <address>
                        <addrLine>
                            <persName key="MAPP0058"><choice><abbr>Mlle.</abbr><expan>Mademoiselle</expan></choice> Monica Stirling</persName>
                        </addrLine>
                            <addrLine>Hotel Mirabeau</addrLine>
                            <addrLine>31 Avenue de la Gard</addrLine>
                            <addrLine>1001 Lausanne</addrLine>
                            <addrLine>Switzerland</addrLine>
                    </address>
                    <salute>
                        Dear Mademoiselle Stirling
                    </salute>
                </opener>
                <p>I refer to correspondence between our <persName key="MAPP0056">Miss Spurdle</persName> <note><p>This probably refers to Rita Spurdle, as that is the only female Spurdle mentioned in the archive.</p></note> and yourself 
            <lb/>regarding the works of <persName key="Q40909">Virginia Woolf</persName> under the title of <title level="m">La Mort
            <lb/>de la Phalene</title> <note><p>Book, written by Virginia Woolf, originally published by <orgName key="Q1623362">The Hogarth Press</orgName> in <placeName>London</placeName>, <date when="1942">1942</date>, then published by Editions du Seuil in Paris, 1968.</p></note>. As a result of her correspondence both with you
            <lb/>and with the French publisher, <orgName key="Q2635075">Editions du Seuil</orgName> <note><p>Editions du Seuil is a French publishing house founded by <persName key="Q3174047">Jean Plaquevent</persName> in 1935.</p></note>, it now seems
            <lb/>clear that an error has occurred over the payment of Royalties.</p>

            <p>In <date when="1968">1968</date>, <persName key="MAPP0054">Madame Arnaud</persName> <note><p>This probably refers to Odette Arnaud, as that is the only female Odette mentioned in the archive.</p></note> instructed the publisher to pay 90&#x25; of
            <lb/>Royalties arising from the book <title level="m">L&apos;Art du Roman</title> <note><p>Book, by Virginia Woolf, published by Editions du Seuil in <placeName>Paris</placeName>, <date when="1963">1963</date>.</p></note> direct to <persName key="Q703935"><choice><abbr>Mr.</abbr><expan>Mister</expan></choice>
            <lb/>Leonard Woolf</persName> and 10&#x25; to <del rend="strikethrough">yourself</del> <add type="handwriting" place="above">her</add>, and this appears to have been
            <lb/>carried out. But no such instruction was given regarding <title level="m">La Mort
            <lb/>de la Phalene</title>. Consequently, <orgName key="Q2635075">Editions du Seuil</orgName> have continued to
            <lb/>pay all Royalties arising from this book, first to <persName key="MAPP0054">Madame Arnaud</persName>&apos;s
            <lb/>agency in <date when="1969">1969</date>, then to <persName key="MAPP0059"><choice><abbr>M.</abbr><expan>Monsieur</expan></choice> Puisoye</persName> <note>This probably refers to Jacques Puisoye, as that is the only male Puisoye mentioned in the archive.</note> as her executor in <date when="1970">1970</date>, <date when="1971">1971</date> and
            <lb/><date when="1972">1972</date>, and in <date when="1973">1973</date> and <date when="1974">1974</date>, to yourself, on the instructions of
            <lb/><persName key="MAPP0059"><choice><abbr>M.</abbr><expan>Monsieur</expan></choice> Puisoye</persName>. The total amount paid was <choice><abbr>Frs.</abbr><expan>Swiss Franc</expan></choice> 1659.97 but in fact
            <lb/>the whole of this amount should have been remitted to the Estate of
            <lb/><persName key="Q40909">Virginia Woolf</persName> except for 10&#x25; to <persName key="MAPP0054">Madame Arnaud</persName> during the time
            <lb/>her agency was still in existence. In fact, however, it appears
            <lb/>that none of this money has ever reached us for the <persName key="Q40909">Woolf</persName> Estate.
            <lb/>We have no means of knowing what happened to the payments which
            <lb/><orgName key="Q2635075">Editions du Seuil</orgName> made to the agency in <date when="1969">1969</date> (<choice><abbr>Frs.</abbr><expan>Swiss Franc</expan></choice> 638.23) nor to
            <lb/>the amount of <choice><abbr>Frs.</abbr><expan>Swiss Franc</expan></choice> 62.05 paid to <persName key="MAPP0059"><choice><abbr>M.</abbr><expan>Monsieur</expan></choice> Puisoye</persName>. But we are informed
            <lb/>by the publishers that for the years <date when="1973">1973</date> and <date when="1974">1974</date> they remitted to
            <lb/>you a total sum of <choice><abbr>Frs.</abbr><expan>Swiss Franc</expan></choice> 959.69. We should be very grateful if you</p>
            <pb/>
            <p>could send us a payment for this sum but in view of the fact that
            <lb/>it does not seem to be possible to contact <persName key="MAPP0059"><choice><abbr>M.</abbr><expan>Monsieur</expan></choice> Puisoye</persName> it would
            <lb/>seem the earlier Royalties due to the Estate cannot now be 
            <lb/>recover<del rend="overwritten">d</del><add place="superimposed">e</add>d.</p>
                <closer>
                    <salute>
                        Yours sincerely
                    </salute>
                    <signed>B.A. Strange
                        <lb/>Company Secretary
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
